# aether-identifier-prefix-convention

Every Aether identifier must carry a mandatory semantic prefix: `~` for mutable variables (Waves), `#` for immutable constants (Anchors), and PascalCase with no prefix for functions/types (Conduits/Molds).

## Procedures
- 1. Prefix every mutable variable with `~` in lowercase-start camelCase: `~count`, `~userInput`. Regex: `~[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*`.
- 2. Prefix every immutable constant with `#` in ALL_CAPS: `#PI`, `#MAX_RETRIES`. Regex: `#[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*`.
- 3. Name all conduit (function) and mold (class) definitions in PascalCase with NO sigil prefix: `Sum`, `UserRecord`. Regex: `[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*`.
- 4. Never rebind an Anchor (`#` identifier) — doing so raises a runtime `StructuralFracture`.
- 5. Method special-names (Init, Echo, Repr, Del, Bool, Len, etc.) follow PascalCase (no prefix), matching conduit conventions.

## Conventions
- The prefix is semantically enforced, not merely stylistic — wrong or missing prefix is a hard error.
- Function parameters are Wave identifiers (`~`) since they are local mutable bindings.
- Special method names defined on Molds use PascalCase: `Init(~self, ...)`, `Echo(~self)`, `Len(~self)`.

